Does the argument icolourswork for you? The control of colours is generally poor in plot.capthist, but I got this:
set.seed(123)
temp <- plot(capt, title = "Individuals per detector", +  type = "n.per.detector", hidetraps = TRUE,
gridspace = 10,border = 1, +  gridlines = TRUE, cappar = list(cex = 1), icolours = topo.colors(10))

